592186444059 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444057 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444059 1079 #uuid "831d751e-c629-5b32-9f44-368844ac1a78" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444060 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444058 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444060 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444060 1077 "field-1" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444060 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444058 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444060 1079 #uuid "a8e8dcc5-5048-58a4-a50f-532f28ef34ce" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444061 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444056 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444061 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444061 1077 "field-1" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444061 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444056 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444061 1079 #uuid "d4f3822a-92a6-5439-9a5d-bf0f8c9a91bb" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444062 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444059 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444062 1069 "q-334936" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444062 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444062 1071 "Given that $P(t)={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(x-3t)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,$ calculate ${P}^{′}(t)$ for $t\\in R$ by differentiating under the integral sign.\n\n${P}^{′}(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444062 1072 #uuid "2a7ae8c6-87fd-5aaa-b1ca-f181d86f7e93" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444062 1074 "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as *differentiating under the integral sign.*\n\nWe wish to compute ${P}^{′}(t),$ where\n\n$$\nP(t)={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(x-3t)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating under the integral sign, we get\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(t)={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(x-3t)^{2}]\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, let's compute the partial derivative with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(x-3t)^{2}] & =2(x-3t)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂t}(x-3t) \\\\  & =2(x-3t)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-6(x-3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this back into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(t) & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}-6(x-3t)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(x-3t)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(x-3t)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-2}^{0}3t\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{-2}^{0}-3tx{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =-2-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(t) & =-6(-2-6t) \\\\  & =12(3t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444063 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444061 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444063 1069 "q-352887" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444063 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444063 1071 "Given that $K(t)={\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,$ calculate ${K}^{′}(t)$ for $t\\in R$ by differentiating under the integral sign.\n\n${K}^{′}(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)(\\,$\n{{field-1}}$)$" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444063 1072 #uuid "5b2ce271-5eac-5d80-b8db-22d863d22bcd" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444063 1074 "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as differentiating under the integral sign.\n\nWe wish to compute ${K}^{′}(t),$ where\n\n$$\nK(t)={\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating under the integral sign, we get\n\n$$\n{K}^{′}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)^{2}]\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, let's compute the partial derivative with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)^{2}] & =2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x) \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this back into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{K}^{′}(t) & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t){\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{4}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,x{|}_{0}^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{K}^{′}(t) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\cdot (4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-24) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444064 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444060 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444064 1069 "q-334973" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444064 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444064 1071 "Given that $P(t)={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,$ calculate ${P}^{′}(t)$ for $t\\in R$ by differentiating under the integral sign.\n\n${P}^{′}(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444064 1072 #uuid "6c38c2df-a1c4-591d-95c2-93cd739693be" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444064 1074 "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as *differentiating under the integral sign.*\n\nWe wish to compute ${P}^{′}(t),$ where\n\n$$\nP(t)={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating under the integral sign, we get\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(t)={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}]\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, let's compute the partial derivative with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}] & =2(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂t}(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =2(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this back into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(t) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t){\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{1}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =0+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t).\n$$" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444065 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444069 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444065 1062 #uuid "0b5c3e8c-b479-5b7c-995d-1b489fe05efc" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444065 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444064 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444066 1062 #uuid "187e39d4-f8d9-5968-b9f2-0918091fc0cc" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444066 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444063 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444067 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444065 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444067 1062 #uuid "452238fc-0a14-5395-9d29-80eea1eaebf3" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444067 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444062 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444068 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444066 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444068 1062 #uuid "86e12b8a-080a-53fd-a5ee-62fcb2d5ac6b" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444068 1063 #edb/ref 17592186311552 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444069 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444068 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444069 1062 #uuid "c87a8b02-417c-5ed5-80b6-82dec3b064cd" 13194139534916 17592186045417 true] [17592186444069 1063 #edb/ref 17592186311550 13194139534916 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-cf6c0bba-9840-5282-9c1e-6b17cae9759d" 17592186444055 "answer-49bfc920-4798-5ac8-829c-10c6425543fd" 17592186444056 "answer-ba4b594e-6e46-5106-afac-33e43b94aed5" 17592186444057 "answer-c3937af2-b650-5eaa-a987-e97fd137f52f" 17592186444058 "answer-field-831d751e-c629-5b32-9f44-368844ac1a78" 17592186444059 "answer-field-a8e8dcc5-5048-58a4-a50f-532f28ef34ce" 17592186444060 "answer-field-d4f3822a-92a6-5439-9a5d-bf0f8c9a91bb" 17592186444061 "question-2a7ae8c6-87fd-5aaa-b1ca-f181d86f7e93" 17592186444062 "question-5b2ce271-5eac-5d80-b8db-22d863d22bcd" 17592186444063 "question-6c38c2df-a1c4-591d-95c2-93cd739693be" 17592186444064 "step-0b5c3e8c-b479-5b7c-995d-1b489fe05efc" 17592